# XVibe — environment TEMPLATE (this file is committed; keep it empty)
#
# ⛔ DO NOT PUT REAL VALUES IN THIS FILE. It is tracked in git, so anything
#    pasted here is published the moment it is pushed — and secret scanners
#    find keys in public repos within minutes.
#
# ✅ Instead:  cp env.example .env.local   →  fill in .env.local
#    Confirm `.env.local` is in .gitignore BEFORE pasting anything into it.
#
# ⚠️ NEVER prefix any of these with NEXT_PUBLIC_ / VITE_ / PUBLIC_ — that ships
#    the secret to every visitor's browser.
#
# If a secret does land somewhere tracked: rotate it, do not just delete the
# line. A Pluggie token is revoked + re-minted in Settings → Tokens; an
# Anthropic key is revoked in the Anthropic console. Deleting the text does not
# un-publish it if it was ever committed.
#
# Deliberately NOT included in this brief: any real token value. Credentials do
# not belong in a docs folder that gets copied between repos. Mint them
# yourself in the Pluggie console (Settings → Tokens) and paste them here.

# ── Pluggie: the builder agent's credential ──────────────────────────────
# mcp-SCOPED token for the project XVibe is building in. Full authoring
# rights over that project: define collections, write entries, mint delivery
# tokens. SERVER-SIDE ONLY.
# Get it: Pluggie console → your project → Settings → Tokens → scope
# "mcp (full)" → Mint. Shown ONCE; only a hash is stored.
#
# FORMAT: the RAW token only — it starts with `agx_`. Do NOT include the word
# "Bearer"; that belongs in the header, and the code builds it:
#     authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.PLUGGIE_MCP_TOKEN}`
# A "Bearer " prefix here produces "Bearer Bearer agx_…" and fails auth.
PLUGGIE_MCP_TOKEN=

# The project this token addresses. Not strictly required (the token itself
# selects the project), but keep it for logging and sanity-checks — confirm it
# matches what get_project_info returns before doing anything credential-shaped.
#
# ID is the full UUID from the admin URL — NOT the shortened `prj_…` display
# form. For the sandbox created 2026-07-26:
#   PLUGGIE_PROJECT_ID=29e647bc-1a7c-43dd-a2e3-6c309f37d021
#   PLUGGIE_PROJECT_NAME=xvibe


# Base URLs. Override only for local/staging Pluggie instances; the generated
# client already defaults to production.
PLUGGIE_MCP_URL=https://pluggie.app/api/mcp
PLUGGIE_DELIVERY_BASE=https://pluggie.app/api/v1

# ── The agent's brain ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Model policy (P0): a router picks the tier per request — Haiku for
# questions/small edits, Sonnet for full builds — and the studio's selector
# can pin a tier per app. XVIBE_FORCE_MODEL (normally unset) overrides
# EVERYTHING with one model id: the operator's cost-emergency brake.
# (BUILDER_MODEL is retired and ignored — delete it from old envs.)
XVIBE_FORCE_MODEL=

# ── Deploy target (Phase 1: static bundles to R2/CDN) ────────────────────
# Fill in when the publish pipeline is built; not needed to start.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET=
# Wildcard domain whose *.<domain> points at the studio host (Render) —
# built apps and previews are served per-app on subdomains of it.
XVIBE_APPS_BASE_DOMAIN=xvibe.app

# ── Hosted-studio settings (Render; leave unset for local dev) ───────────
# Gate the studio behind a passphrase — builds spend ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, so a
# public, ungated studio is an open wallet. Unset = no gate (local dev).
STUDIO_ACCESS_KEY=
# Persistent state dir (Render disk mount). Unset = ./.xvibe
XVIBE_STATE_DIR=

# ── NOT here on purpose ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The DELIVERY token for a built app is minted at build time by the agent
# (mint_delivery_token) and written into THAT app's environment — never into
# XVibe's own env, and never into a generated client's source.
